From 7775c1ffc16b13cd84b1eecc360db77526405d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:49:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(units): status lines, refusals and the gate's gouge
 clause speak the document's units

Tier 1 of #578: transient strings - the ones that quote the numbers the user is already reading - now format through app::units::of(world) and the pure geometry::units formatters, so an inch document hears inches. New vol formatter mirrors area (inches get three extra decimals); Unit::vol_suffix gains the superscript spellings so mm sentences stay byte-identical. deviate_readout takes a Unit like its sibling sim_readout. Persisted notes (tier 2) wait for the structured-note pattern; machine-limit and pure-crate refusals stay put - docs/decisions/578-units-in-errors.md keeps the reasons.
